1.  A DWARF INSIDE A CLUSTER -- the Coma UDGs (h9).  Two corrections: the prescription, and the ARGUMENT of nu
==============================================================================================================================
  h9's Coma model: M200 = 1.30e+15, c = 5.0, R200 = 2900 kpc  ->  R500 = 1383 kpc, M500 = 6.98e+14 Msun
  the UDGs sit at mean 3-D radii 868-2336 kpc = 0.63-1.69 R500

  the baryon fraction that sets the NEWTONIAN external field, measured from the 12 X-COP clusters on disk
  (M500 = 3.5-9e14, i.e. Coma-like) rather than assumed:
   r/R500              f_gas   M_star/M_gas    f_bar    N
     0.30   0.1099 [0.0917,0.1182]         0.0660   0.1171   12
     0.40   0.1228 [0.0996,0.1298]         0.0506   0.1290   12
     0.50   0.1290 [0.1074,0.1413]         0.0466   0.1350   12
     0.60   0.1340 [0.1095,0.1471]         0.0457   0.1401   12
     0.80   0.1415 [0.1236,0.1546]         0.0427   0.1475   11
     1.00   0.1477 [0.1333,0.1596]         0.0446   0.1543   11
     1.20   0.1494 [0.1379,0.1570]         0.0541   0.1575    8
  [PASS] 1a the baryon fraction is MEASURED, not chosen: 12 X-COP clusters give it as a monotonically rising function of radius over 0.3-1.2 R500, in the range a cluster baryon budget has to be in.  AGAINST INTEREST -- and this is why the check is written to be able to catch it -- at 1.2 R500 the measured f_bar slightly EXCEEDS the cosmic value 0.157, i.e. the measurement gives the LARGEST external field the framework could face, which is the least favourable choice for the framework and not the most   (f_bar rises monotonically 0.117 -> 0.158 over 0.3-1.2 R500; f_bar(0.3) = 0.117, f_bar(1.0) = 0.154, f_bar(1.2) = 0.158 vs cosmic 0.157)

  THE THREE DEFENSIBLE EXTERNAL FIELDS at a UDG's position, all from the same measured cluster:
    (T) the TRUE dynamical field  g_ext = G M_NFW(<r)/r^2                     -- what h9 fed to nu.  WRONG in QUMOND:
        nu takes the NEWTONIAN field of the real matter, and in this framework the real matter is baryons.
    (M) the KERNEL-INVERTED field: the Newtonian g_N with nu(g_N/a0) g_N = the MEASURED true field.  This is the
        observationally anchored choice -- it uses the measured cluster acceleration and the kernel's own inverse.
    (B) the BARYON-CONSISTENT field  g_N = f_bar(r/R500) x G M_NFW(<r)/r^2    -- the framework's own matter content.
    (M) and (B) differ by exactly the standing cluster residual: the framework cannot make Coma's own field from
        Coma's own baryons, so this liability leaks into every EFE calculation done inside a cluster.
  UDG                       r/R500  f_bar  x_ext(T)  x_ext(M)  x_ext(B)
  DF44                        1.69  0.158    0.3013    0.0701    0.0475
  DFX1                        1.44  0.158    0.3634    0.0974    0.0572
  J125848.94+281037.1         0.82  0.148    0.6656    0.2695    0.0986
  J125904.06+281422.4         0.82  0.148    0.6603    0.2661    0.0979
  J125904.20+281507.7         0.83  0.149    0.6516    0.2604    0.0969
  J125929.89+274303.0         0.79  0.147    0.6896    0.2854    0.1014
  J125937.23+274815.2         0.69  0.144    0.7740    0.3431    0.1112
  J130005.40+275333.0         0.63  0.141    0.8461    0.3947    0.1194
  J130026.26+272735.2         1.09  0.156    0.4976    0.1669    0.0775
  J130028.34+274820.5         0.74  0.145    0.7300    0.3126    0.1061
  J130038.63+272835.3         1.09  0.156    0.4988    0.1676    0.0777
  [PASS] 1b the cluster residual, seen from inside the EFE.  The Newtonian field Coma's measured acceleration REQUIRES (M) is larger than the Newtonian field Coma's measured baryons SUPPLY (B) by a factor that is the standing cluster liability itself.  It is quoted here so that the Coma UDG numbers below are read as CONDITIONAL on which of the two is used, and not as a free choice   (median g_N(kernel-inverted)/g_N(baryons) = 2.72; the ledger's cluster rows need x1.45-x3.45 in acceleration, and this is the same number arriving by a different route)

  footing canonical:   inverse-variance mean log10(g_obs/g_pred), 11 Coma UDGs
  external field            isolated (EFE o  naive nu(y_e)    sum-in-nu     [  eq.60 parallel   FLUX THEOREM (e
  T true dynamical                   +0.396           +1.195           +1.197           +1.375           +1.247
  M kernel-inverted                  +0.396           +1.021           +1.030           +1.245           +1.083
